C alarm limit of 2\'b0F/second with a period of execution of 100 ms, and an analog input module with a resolution of 1\'b0F, then every time the input value changes, a ROC alarm is generated because the instruction sees a rate of 10\'b0
F/second. However, by entering a PVROCPeriod of at least 1 sec, the ROC alarm is only generated if the rate truly exceeds the 2\'b0F/second limit.
